.TH SWAYDESK-LANGUAGE 1 2026-11-19 "swaydesk 0.1.6" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-language \- keyboard layout for Waybar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-language
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints one Waybar line (JSON) with the active keyboard layout's short name, such as br or us, and a new line each time the layout or the keyboards change. It follows Sway's input events over the IPC socket (SWAYSOCK) and runs until Sway exits.
.PP
Only real keyboards count: virtual keyboards (wtype, on\-screen keyboards, remote access: the ones wlroots creates, with vendor and product 0:0) are ignored. With fewer than two layouts, the line's text is empty and Waybar hides the module. The short names come from the xkb registry (/usr/share/X11/xkb/rules/evdev.xml); two layouts with the same short name are numbered, such as us1 and us2.
.PP
The session runs it under the name waybar\-language (a link in the package's helper directory to /usr/bin/swaydesk\-language), as Waybar's custom/language module; a click switches to the next layout with swaymsg.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 at once without doing anything: the Python launchers use it to check that the binary and its libraries load.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SWAYSOCK
Sway's IPC socket. Without it, the module prints an empty line and exits with 1.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/X11/xkb/rules/evdev.xml
The xkb registry, for the layouts' short names (and evdev.extras.xml, when present).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swaydesk (7),
.BR sway\-input (5),
.BR waybar (5)
